格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"DSH plugin bundle: scan a QR to open the deepseek-harness web UI on your phone inside the same session - cloudflared quick tunnel, no database, Windows/macOS/Linux","id":"gh:1349090911","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-remote-tunnel-easy","slug":"Raiyan007-gb/dsh-remote-tunnel-easy","topics":["cloudflared","deepseek","deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","dsh-plugin-market","dsh-plugins","qrcode"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"DSH plugin bundle: scan a QR to open the deepseek-harness web UI on your phone inside the same sessi"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"on - cloudflared quick tunnel, no database, Windows/macOS/Linux"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-remote-tunnel-easy"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**Open your DeepSeek Harness session on your phone — by pointing the camera at it.**"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Scan the QR in **Settings → Plugins** and the harness opens in your phone's\nbrowser, *inside the ses"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"sion you are already working in*. Same workspace, same\nchat. No typing a URL. The `dsh web` terminal"},{"id":"p4s3","text":"eady working in*. Same workspace, same\nchat. No typing a URL. The `dsh web` terminal prints nothing."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"> **⚠️ Renamed from `qrcode-hassle-free`** — previously `Raiyan007-gb/dsh-qrcode-hassle-free` (npm `"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"qrcode-hassle-free`). Now **`dsh-remote-tunnel-easy`** (`Raiyan007-gb/dsh-remote-tunnel-easy`, npm `"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"dsh-remote-tunnel-easy@1.4.2`). If you installed the old name, migrate first — remove the old bundle"},{"id":"p5s4","text":", then add the new one."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"A one-command **DeepSeek Harness web bundle** that brings QR-based remote\nhandoff to the Settings pa"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"ge. It starts a `cloudflared` quick tunnel, loops\nyour phone into the exact session the desktop is u"},{"id":"p6s3","text":"sing, and draws the QR code\nplus settings right next to your other plugins — no terminal noise, no\nd"},{"id":"p6s4","text":"atabase, no Firebase, no app install."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"- **Scan to open** — a real QR code in **Settings → Plugins**, fresh every run\n- **Same session** — "},{"id":"p7s2","text":"the phone lands inside the chat and workspace you are already in\n- **Self-installing** — detects `cl"},{"id":"p7s3","text":"oudflared`, and downloads it (SHA-256 verified) when missing\n- **Regenerate** — one click mints a fr"},{"id":"p7s4","text":"esh tunnel URL for the same session, without restarting\n- **Editable settings** — tunnel target, `cl"},{"id":"p7s5","text":"oudflared` path, and session handoff from the page\n- **Nothing stored** — the tunnel URL is random p"},{"id":"p7s6","text":"er run; nothing is saved anywhere\n- **Everywhere** — Windows (x64/x86), macOS (Intel/Apple Silicon),"},{"id":"p7s7","text":" and Linux (x64/arm64)"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"## At a Glance"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"| Question | Answer |"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"| **What is it?** | A `dsh` bundle that shows a scannable QR code and access link in the Settings pa"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"ge, so a phone opens the harness inside the active session. |\n| **Who is it for?** | Anyone running "},{"id":"p10s3","text":"`dsh web` who wants their phone on the same session without typing tunnel URLs and tokens. |\n| **Wha"},{"id":"p10s4","text":"t do I get?** | A loopback edge proxy, a `cloudflared` quick tunnel, same-session handoff, and a liv"},{"id":"p10s5","text":"e QR + settings card in **Settings → Plugins**. |\n| **What does it run on?** | Windows, macOS, and L"},{"id":"p10s6","text":"inux — anything `dsh` runs on. |\n| **Is cloud required?** | No account or signup. `cloudflared` is u"},{"id":"p10s7","text":"sed, and auto-downloaded on first run when missing; the tunnel is public, and the token in the link "},{"id":"p10s8","text":"downloaded on first run when missing; the tunnel is public, and the token in the link is the gate. |"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"## Get Started"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"Run `dsh web` once so a profile exists — that is the only prerequisite.\n`cloudflared` is no longer s"},{"id":"p12s2","text":"omething you install by hand: on first tunnel start\nthe bundle probes your `PATH`, and when no `clou"},{"id":"p12s3","text":"dflared` is found it downloads\nthe official pinned binary (SHA-256 verified), caches it under your u"},{"id":"p12s4","text":"ser cache\ndirectory, and reuses it from then on. Prefer your own install? Put it on\n`PATH`, or set t"},{"id":"p12s5","text":"he **cloudflared path** field in the card to an absolute path —\nan explicit path disables both probi"},{"id":"p12s6","text":"th** field in the card to an absolute path —\nan explicit path disables both probing and downloading."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"The simplest path — install from the npm registry with the plugin name:"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"The `--config.minimumReleaseAge=0` flag bypasses pnpm's ~24-hour release-age\ngate, so a freshly publ"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"ished version installs immediately. Without it, a plain\n`dsh plugin --profile web add dsh-remote-tun"},{"id":"p15s3","text":"nel-easy` still works but may hold off\nuntil the freshness window lapses."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"## What it does"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"On every `dsh web` start the bundle:"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"1. Spawns a loopback edge proxy (127.0.0.1, ephemeral port) that forwards every\nrequest and WebSocke"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"t upgrade to the harness, rewriting `Host` and `Origin`\nto the loopback authority. This is what make"},{"id":"p19s3","text":"s the harness's `/api`\nbrowser-trust fence accept tunneled traffic — the fence requires\n`Origin == H"},{"id":"p19s4","text":"ost`, and a phone's `Origin` is the tunnel hostname, which\n`--http-host-header` rewriting alone can "},{"id":"p19s5","text":"never satisfy. Without the proxy\nthe app loads but every API call 403s.\n2. Locates `cloudflared` — t"},{"id":"p19s6","text":"he configured **cloudflared path** override, else a\nbinary on `PATH`, else a pinned download (`2026."},{"id":"p19s7","text":"8.2`) SHA-256 verified and\ncached under the user cache directory. It then spawns\n`cloudflared tunnel"},{"id":"p19s8","text":" --no-autoupdate --url http://127.0.0.1:<proxy-port>`\npointed at that proxy.\n3. Waits for cloudflare"},{"id":"p19s9","text":"d to print the random `https://<name>.trycloudflare.com` URL.\n4. Resolves this process's launch toke"},{"id":"p19s10","text":"n via the harness connection service\n(`authenticatedUrl` — the same mint the console line prints).\n5"},{"id":"p19s11","text":". Seeds the most recently active session id into every served index page (via\nthe webserver's index-"},{"id":"p19s12","text":"injection table), gated to non-loopback origins and\nonce per tab — so any tunnel entry lands inside "},{"id":"p19s13","text":"the session the desktop is\nworking in. The id is resolved on the Host at render time (cached, refres"},{"id":"p19s14","text":"hed\nevery 15s); the phone makes no `/api` call for the seed itself.\n6. Registers a token-gated `/rem"},{"id":"p19s15","text":"ote-handoff` route as a fallback entry path:\nsame seeding, then the normal token→cookie login (SHA-2"},{"id":"p19s16","text":"56 constant-time\ncompare). Prefix-matched, so `/remote-handoff` and `/remote-handoff/` both work.\n7."},{"id":"p19s17","text":" Registers a `remote-handoff` settings namespace and a loopback-only bridge\n(`/api/dsh-remote-handof"},{"id":"p19s18","text":"f-settings`). The card in **Settings → Plugins →\nDSH Remote** reads the tunnel status (QR matrix + a"},{"id":"p19s19","text":"ccess link) from that\nbridge and draws them in the page, alongside the editable `tunnelTarget` /\n`cl"},{"id":"p19s20","text":"oudflaredPath` / `sessionHandoff` settings. The **Regenerate** button\nrestarts the tunnel in place f"},{"id":"p19s21","text":"or a brand-new URL on the same session, and an\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"## Requirements"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"- No manual `cloudflared` install — downloaded automatically when missing\n(Windows x64/x86, macOS In"},{"id":"p21s2","text":"tel/Apple Silicon, Linux x64/arm64); any other\nplatform needs a `cloudflared` on `PATH` or an explic"},{"id":"p21s3","text":"it **cloudflared path**.\n- Network access on first run (to reach GitHub for the binary download)\n- N"},{"id":"p21s4","text":"ode — already present where `dsh` runs\n- Phone on any network — the tunnel is public; the token in t"},{"id":"p21s5","text":"he URL is the only\ngate, so treat the shown link like a password."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
